// Granted onto the CASTER by IronShoulderSkillAction's own Begin phase and reset to empty every
// activation - remembers which enemies already got knocked back this dash so a target that keeps
// pace inside the check box across OnGoing ticks only gets launched once, not once per tick. Damage
// still repeats every tick it's caught (see IronShoulderSkillAction) - same "damage repeats, a
// one-shot knockback doesn't" convention HitPathSkillAction.HitAroundCaster documents for its own
// OnGoing mode, just enforced here instead of left to chance.
//
// Capacity is small since the box only ever catches a handful of enemies within one activation -
// once full, any further new enemy simply isn't deduped (falls back to the pre-existing behavior),
// an accepted limitation rather than a silent bug. Lives as its own component rather than growing
// SkillSlot/CharacterSkills - see CharacterSkills.qtn's own ProjectilePending comment for why an
// EntityRef field was deliberately kept off that struct (Quantum's Unity-prototype codegen silently
// drops the Upgrades array from the Inspector once CharacterSkills holds any EntityRef).
component IronShoulderHitTracker
{
    array<EntityRef>[8] HitEntities;
    Byte HitCount;
}
